Jahshaka patch 0029 — a surface takes a reflection probe's picture only if it
is IN that picture.

WHY (owner, 2026-09-13, REFLECTION_PROBE_AUDIT.md Q2): "why would the outside of
a building show the room inside? That makes zero sense to me." — and when the
lead reached for enclosure detection: "the engine should not know if there is a
room? Isn't it the layout of objects in a scene that matters?" Correct: the
engine has no concept of a room, only geometry and where it stands.

At this pin the only spatial tests are two AXIS-ALIGNED BOXES: the parallax box
(`getProbeFade > 0`) and the influence area (`getProbeNDF`). Neither traces
geometry, both carry margins (the grid overlap overruns the region by 12.5% of a
cell, `CubemapProbe::set` pads x1.005, our own shape clamp pads x1.05), and after
Jahshaka's A2 shape clamp the parallax box is ~the whole probe region indoors —
so the entry gate excludes nothing there. The outward face of a slab whose inward
face a probe photographed is, geometrically, inside the same box.

THE RULE IS VISIBILITY FROM THE PROBE, and the probe already captured the answer.
The DepthCompressor pass writes `min( 0.5 * fDist / fApproxDist, 1 )` into the
cube's ALPHA for every texel (Media/2.0/scripts/materials/Common/Any/
PccDepthCompressor_ps.any), where fApproxDist is the probe camera's distance to
its own parallax box along that direction. Upstream's `getPccVctBlendWeight`
already decodes exactly that (`* (pccCompressedDepth * 2.0)`, Vct_piece_ps.any),
and the IBL convolution preserves alpha (SpecularIblIntegrator_piece_cs.any:
`alphaValue += sampleValue.a * NoL`), so mip 0 of the bound array is the probe's
depth. This patch marches from the probe camera towards the shaded point, reads
what the probe saw that way, and treats "it saw something nearer" as occlusion.
It is the same Chebyshev-style test the irradiance field already applies to its
own probes.

CONFIDENCE SCALES THE CONTRIBUTION, NOT THE WEIGHT — the measured trap from lane
E3, and the reason this patch keeps TWO weights. `pccEnvS` is normalised by
`cubemapAccumWeight` at the bottom of the piece, so crushing every probe's weight
would only renormalise the same probes back to full strength. So the visibility
factor is folded into `probeFade` (which multiplies every sampled term, and
patch 0017's probe-trust accumulator with it) while `cubemapAccumWeight` keeps
accumulating the FULL, unscaled weight — one added local and one changed line.
With

    w_p = probeFade, v_p = visibility, t_p = PCC trust, W = sum( w_p )
    pccEnvS    = sum( w_p * v_p * t_p * S_p ) / W
    trust      = sum( w_p * v_p * t_p ) / W          (patch 0017's accumVctLerp)
    envColourS = pccEnvS + prior * (1 - trust)       (patch 0017's blend)

the share an occluded probe does not claim goes back to whatever filled
`envColourS` before the probes ran — cone tracing, the irradiance field, the sky
— and never to black, which is the failure mode a naive tightening of probe
influence produces in a sealed room. With every probe fully visible (v_p = 1)
every line is bit-identical to the code it replaces.

THE NON-VCT BRANCH at the bottom of the piece is deliberately left alone: it has
no other environment term to hand the unclaimed share back to, so there the
occluded share simply drops out. Jahshaka never takes it (a probe grid exists
only in the VCT+PCC hybrid, so `vct_num_probes` is always set when probes are),
and touching that line would break `git apply --reverse --check` of patch 0017,
which build-ogre.sh uses as its already-applied test.

SLACK. Relative, because the error is: one cube texel spans a solid angle, the
compressed depth is 8 bits at the LDR tiers, and a texel straddling a silhouette
filters between two depths. 8% of the probe-to-point distance with a floor of 2%
of the captured distance keeps grazing floors and walls fully visible; the case
the owner pointed at (a slab's outward face, ~1 m past the inward face a probe
2.7 m away photographed) fails it by more than 30%.

COST: one extra cube-array fetch at mip 0 per probe per pixel inside the loop —
which patch 0028 has just removed from every material with no specular response.

MEDIA-ONLY (Hlms .any templates, both CRLF — edited in binary mode). Studio
stages media from the SOURCE tree, so every tree still needs the patch loop /
build-ogre.sh; no C++ is rebuilt by it.

Covered by tests/gi/test_gi_probe_visibility.cpp (gi.probe_visibility).
--- a/Samples/Media/Hlms/Common/Any/Cubemap_piece_all.any
+++ b/Samples/Media/Hlms/Common/Any/Cubemap_piece_all.any
@@ -99,6 +99,31 @@
 	return min( min( vDiff.x, vDiff.y ), vDiff.z );
 }
 
+/** Jahshaka patch 0029 -- HOW FAR THE PROBE COULD SEE IN THIS DIRECTION.
+
+	The probe's own capture carries its depth: the DepthCompressor pass writes
+	`min( 0.5 * fDist / fApproxDist, 1 )` into the cube's ALPHA, where
+	fApproxDist is the distance from the probe camera to its parallax box along
+	that same direction (Common/Any/PccDepthCompressor_ps.any). This is the
+	exact inverse of that encoding, and it is what upstream's own
+	getPccVctBlendWeight already assumes (`interesectionPosVS = cubemapPosVS +
+	(...) * (pccCompressedDepth * 2.0)`, Vct_piece_ps.any).
+
+	dirLS must be NORMALISED and in the probe's local space; the return value is
+	a distance in that same space, saturating at 2 * fApproxDist (the encoding's
+	own ceiling, i.e. "at least this far").
+*/
+INLINE midf probeCapturedDistance( midf3 dirLS, midf3 cameraPosLS, midf3 probeShapeHalfSize,
+								   midf compressedDepth )
+{
+	midf3 invDirLS = midf3_c( 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ) / dirLS;
+	midf3 atMinPlane = ( -probeShapeHalfSize - cameraPosLS ) * invDirLS;
+	midf3 atMaxPlane = (  probeShapeHalfSize - cameraPosLS ) * invDirLS;
+	midf3 largest = max( atMaxPlane.xyz, atMinPlane.xyz );
+	midf approxDist = min( min( largest.x, largest.y ), largest.z );
+	return compressedDepth * _h( 2.0 ) * approxDist;
+}
+
 INLINE midf getProbeNDF( midf3 posLS, midf3 probeToAreaCenterOffsetLS,
 						 midf3 innerRange, midf3 outerRange )
 {
--- a/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/ForwardPlus_DecalsCubemaps_piece_ps.any
+++ b/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/ForwardPlus_DecalsCubemaps_piece_ps.any
@@ -193,6 +193,78 @@
 			probeFade = probeFade * probeFade;
 			probeFade *= midf_c( probePriority );
 
+			// ---- JAHSHAKA PATCH 0029: CAN THIS POINT SEE THE PROBE? ----------
+			//
+			// Owner, 2026-09-13: "why would the outside of a building show the
+			// room inside? That makes zero sense to me." -- and, when the lead
+			// reached for enclosure detection: "the engine should not know if
+			// there is a room? Isn't it the layout of objects in a scene that
+			// matters?" Exactly so. A probe is a photograph taken from a point,
+			// and the only honest question is whether the shaded point is IN
+			// that photograph or hidden behind something in it. Pure geometry;
+			// no concept of a room required.
+			//
+			// The probe already captured the answer. Its cube's ALPHA is how far
+			// it could see in every direction (the DepthCompressor pass), so:
+			// march from the probe camera towards this pixel, read what the
+			// probe saw that way, and treat "it saw something nearer" as
+			// occlusion. The parallax box (getProbeFade, above) stays as the
+			// cheap first rejection; this is the test that knows about geometry.
+			//
+			// THE SLACK IS RELATIVE, because the error is: one cube texel spans
+			// a solid angle, the compressed depth is 8 bits at the LDR tiers,
+			// and a texel straddling a silhouette filters between two depths.
+			// 8% of the probe-to-point distance, floored at 2% of the captured
+			// distance, keeps grazing floors and walls fully visible while the
+			// case the owner pointed at -- the outward face of a slab whose
+			// inward face the probe photographed -- fails it by 30% or more.
+			midf3 probeCamPosLS   = midf3_c( probe.cubemapPosLS.xyz );
+			midf3 probeToPosLS    = posInProbSpace.xyz - probeCamPosLS;
+			midf  probeToPosDist  = length( probeToPosLS );
+			midf3 probeToPosDirLS = probeToPosLS / max( probeToPosDist, _h( 1e-6 ) );
+			// The cube is sampled LEFT HANDED (localCorrect flips z on the way
+			// out); the visibility ray is flipped the same way.
+			midf3 probeVisDirLS   = midf3_c( probeToPosDirLS.x, probeToPosDirLS.y,
+											 -probeToPosDirLS.z );
+			midf  probeVisDepth;
+			@property( !hlms_cubemaps_use_dpm )
+				probeVisDepth = OGRE_SampleArrayCubeLevelF16(
+					texEnvProbeMap, samplerState@value(envMapRegSampler),
+					float3( probeVisDirLS ), probeCubemapIdx, 0.0 ).w;
+			@else
+				probeVisDepth = OGRE_SampleArray2DLevelF16(
+					texEnvProbeMap, samplerState@value(envMapRegSampler),
+					mapCubemapToDpm( probeVisDirLS ), probeCubemapIdx, 0.0 ).w;
+			@end
+			midf probeSeenDist = probeCapturedDistance( probeToPosDirLS, probeCamPosLS,
+														midf3_c( probe.halfSize.xyz ),
+														probeVisDepth );
+			midf probeVisSlack = max( probeToPosDist * _h( 0.08 ),
+									  probeSeenDist * _h( 0.02 ) );
+			midf probeVisible = saturate( ( probeSeenDist - probeToPosDist + probeVisSlack ) /
+										  max( probeVisSlack, _h( 1e-6 ) ) );
+
+			// CONFIDENCE SCALES THE CONTRIBUTION, NOT THE WEIGHT -- the measured
+			// trap from lane E3, and the reason this is two variables rather
+			// than one. `pccEnvS` is normalised by cubemapAccumWeight at the
+			// bottom of this piece, so crushing every probe's weight would only
+			// renormalise the SAME probes back to full strength. So `probeFade`
+			// (which multiplies every sampled term below, and patch 0017's
+			// probe-trust accumulator with it) carries the visibility, while
+			// cubemapAccumWeight keeps accumulating the FULL weight. The share
+			// an occluded probe does not claim is then handed back by patch
+			// 0017's blend to whatever filled envColourS before the probes ran
+			// -- cone tracing, the irradiance field, the sky -- and never to
+			// black, which is what a naive tightening of probe influence
+			// produces in a sealed room.
+			//
+			// In the non-VCT branch at the bottom (upstream-only: Jahshaka
+			// builds a probe grid in the VCT+PCC hybrid alone, so vct_num_probes
+			// is always set when probes exist) there is no other environment
+			// term to hand it back to, and the occluded share simply drops out.
+			midf probeFadeFull = probeFade;
+			probeFade = probeFade * probeVisible;
+
 			@property( vct_num_probes )
 				midf4 reflDirLS_dist = localCorrect( pixelData.reflDir, posInProbSpace, probe );
 				midf3 reflDirLS = reflDirLS_dist.xyz;
@@ -274,7 +346,7 @@
 				clearCoatPccEnvS += clearCoatPccSingleEnvS;
 			@end
 
-			cubemapAccumWeight += probeFade;
+			cubemapAccumWeight += probeFadeFull;	// Jahshaka patch 0029 -- FULL weight
 		}
 	}
 
